{"id":"mahabharata-8-018","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":18,"title":"अष्टादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 18 · Uluka and Satanika; Panchala heroes fall","summary":{"en":"Uluka attacks Yuyutsu, and Uluka's weapons cut down the Panchala chiefs one by one as Karna drives on. The Pandava army, with Gautama's son Shatanika defeated, flees.","kn":"ಉಲೂಕ ಯುಯುತ್ಸುವಿನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕರ್ಣ ಮುನ್ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಿದ್ದಂತೆ ಪಾಂಚಾಲ ಮುಖ್ಯರು ಒಬ್ಬೊಬ್ಬರಾಗಿ ಬೀಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಶತಾನೀಕ ಸೋತಾಗ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಓಡುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"उलूक युयुत्सु पर आक्रमण करता है और कर्ण के आगे बढ़ने पर पाञ्चाल प्रमुख एक-एक कर गिरते हैं। शतानीक के पराजित होने पर पाण्डव सेना भाग खड़ी होती है।","te":"ఉలూకుడు యుయుత్సునిపై దాడి చేస్తాడు; కర్ణుడు సాగుతుండగా పాంచాల నాయకులు ఒక్కొక్కరే పడతారు. శతానీకుడు ఓడగా పాండవసేన పారిపోతుంది.","ta":"உலூகன் யுயுத்சுவைத் தாக்க, கர்ணன் முன்னேறுகையில் பாஞ்சாலத் தலைவர் ஒவ்வொருவராக வீழ்கின்றனர். சதானீகன் தோற்க, பாண்டவப் படை ஓடுகிறது.","ml":"ഉലൂകൻ യുയുത്സുവിനെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; കർണ്ണൻ മുന്നേറുമ്പോൾ ഉലൂകന്റെ ആയുധങ്ങൾ പാഞ്ചാല നായകരെ ഓരോരുത്തരായി വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു. ഗൗതമന്റെ പുത്രൻ ശതാനീകൻ തോറ്റതോടെ പാണ്ഡവസേന ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.18; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"युयुत्सुं तव पुत्रं तु प्राद्रवन्तं महद्बलम् ।\nउलूकोऽभ्यपतत्तूर्णं तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As your son Yuyutsu, leading a great force, was advancing, Uluka swiftly attacked him, shouting, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":2,"text":"युयुत्सुस्तु ततो राजञ्शितधारेण पत्रिणा ।\nउलूकं ताडयामास वज्रेणेन्द्र इवाचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, Yuyutsu struck Uluka with a sharp-edged arrow, as Indra strikes a mountain with the thunderbolt."}},{"n":3,"text":"उलूकस्तु ततः क्रुद्धस्तव पुत्रस्य संयुगे ।\nक्षुरप्रेण धनुश्छित्त्वा ताडयामास कर्णिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Uluka, angry in the battle, cut your son's bow with a razor-headed arrow and hit him with a barbed arrow."}},{"n":4,"text":"तदपास्य धनुश्छिन्नं युयुत्सुर्वेगवत्तरम् ।\nअन्यदादत्त सुमहच्चापं संरक्तलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yuyutsu threw aside the cut bow, and with reddened eyes took up another, much greater and swifter bow."}},{"n":5,"text":"शाकुनिं च ततः षष्ट्या विव्याध भरतर्षभ ।\nसारथिं त्रिभिरानर्छत्तं च भूयो व्यविध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O best of the Bharatas, he pierced Shakuni's son with sixty arrows, hit his charioteer with three, and pierced Uluka again."}},{"n":6,"text":"उलूकस्तं तु विंशत्या विद्ध्वा हेमविभूषितैः ।\nअथास्य समरे क्रुद्धो ध्वजं चिच्छेद काञ्चनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Uluka pierced him with twenty gold-adorned arrows, and then, angry in battle, cut down his golden standard."}},{"n":7,"text":"स च्छिन्नयष्टिः सुमहाञ्शीर्यमाणो महाध्वजः ।\nपपात प्रमुखे राजन्युयुत्सोः काञ्चनोज्ज्वलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great standard, its staff cut, broke apart and fell, shining with gold, right in front of Yuyutsu, O king."}},{"n":8,"text":"ध्वजमुन्मथितं दृष्ट्वा युयुत्सुः क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nउलूकं पञ्चभिर्बाणैराजघान स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his standard torn down, Yuyutsu, dizzy with anger, struck Uluka between the breasts with five arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"उलूकस्तस्य भल्लेन तैलधौतेन मारिष ।\nशिरश्चिच्छेद सहसा यन्तुर्भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"O sir, best of the Bharatas, Uluka suddenly cut off the head of Yuyutsu's charioteer with an oil-washed broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":10,"text":"जघान चतुरोऽश्वांश्च तं च विव्याध पञ्चभिः ।\nसोऽतिविद्धो बलवता प्रत्यपायाद्रथान्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also killed his four horses and pierced Yuyutsu with five arrows. Badly wounded by the strong Uluka, Yuyutsu withdrew to another chariot."}},{"n":11,"text":"तं निर्जित्य रणे राजन्नुलूकस्त्वरितो ययौ ।\nपाञ्चालान्सृञ्जयांश्चैव विनिघ्नन्निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated him in battle, O king, Uluka went swiftly on, killing Panchalas and Srinjayas with sharp arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"शतानीकं महाराज श्रुतकर्मा सुतस्तव ।\nव्यश्वसूतरथं चक्रे निमेषार्धादसंभ्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Shrutakarman, O great king, left Shatanika without horses, charioteer or chariot, in half the blink of an eye, without any hurry."}},{"n":13,"text":"हताश्वे तु रथे तिष्ठञ्शतानीको महाबलः ।\nगदां चिक्षेप संक्रुद्धस्तव पुत्रस्य मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standing in his chariot with its horses killed, the mighty Shatanika, furious, hurled his mace at your son, O sir."}},{"n":14,"text":"सा कृत्वा स्यन्दनं भस्म हयांश्चैव ससारथीन् ।\nपपात धरणीं तूर्णं दारयन्तीव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mace turned the chariot, its horses and charioteer to ashes, and then fell swiftly to the ground as though splitting it, O Bharata."}},{"n":15,"text":"तावुभौ विरथौ वीरौ कुरूणां कीर्तिवर्धनौ ।\nअपाक्रमेतां युद्धार्तौ प्रेक्षमाणौ परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both those heroes, chariotless, increasers of the Kurus' fame, pained by the fight, drew back, looking at each other."}},{"n":16,"text":"पुत्रस्तु तव संभ्रान्तो विवित्सो रथमाविशत् ।\nशतानीकोऽपि त्वरितः प्रतिविन्ध्यरथं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son, bewildered, boarded Vivitsu's chariot, and Shatanika too quickly went to Pratavindhya's chariot."}},{"n":17,"text":"सुतसोमस्तु शकुनिं विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ।\nनाकम्पयत संरब्धो वार्योघ इव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sutasoma pierced Shakuni with sharp arrows, but could not shake him, who stood firm like a mountain against a flood of water."}},{"n":18,"text":"सुतसोमस्तु तं दृष्ट्वा पितुरत्यन्तवैरिणम् ।\nशरैरनेकसाहस्रैश्छादयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sutasoma, seeing the man who was his father's bitter enemy, O Bharata, covered him with many thousands of arrows."}},{"n":19,"text":"ताञ्शराञ्शकुनिस्तूर्णं चिच्छेदान्यैः पतत्रिभिः ।\nलघ्वस्त्रश्चित्रयोधी च जितकाशी च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, light-handed with weapons, a varied fighter and always victorious in battle, quickly cut those arrows with other arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"निवार्य समरे चापि शरांस्तान्निशितैः शरैः ।\nआजघान सुसंक्रुद्धः सुतसोमं त्रिभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having beaten those arrows back in battle with sharp arrows, he was very angry and struck Sutasoma with three arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्याश्वान्केतनं सूतं तिलशो व्यधमच्छरैः ।\nस्यालस्तव महावीर्यस्ततस्ते चुक्रुशुर्जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your brother-in-law of great prowess ground Sutasoma's horses, banner and charioteer to bits with arrows, and the people cried out."}},{"n":22,"text":"हताश्वो विरथश्चैव छिन्नधन्वा च मारिष ।\nधन्वी धनुर्वरं गृह्य रथाद्भूमावतिष्ठत ।\nव्यसृजत्सायकांश्चैव स्वर्णपुङ्खाञ्शिलाशितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his horses killed, chariotless and his bow cut, O sir, that bowman took a fine bow and stood on the ground out of the chariot, and shot gold-feathered, stone-sharpened arrows."}},{"n":23,"text":"छादयामासुरथ ते तव स्यालस्य तं रथम् ।\nपतंगानामिव व्राताः शरव्राता महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows covered your brother-in-law's chariot, as swarms of moths cover a great chariot-warrior."}},{"n":24,"text":"रथोपस्थान्समीक्ष्यापि विव्यथे नैव सौबलः ।\nप्रमृद्नंश्च शरांस्तांस्ताञ्शरव्रातैर्महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though he saw them in his chariot's seat, Shakuni, the famous son of Subala, was not shaken, and crushed those arrows with his own volleys."}},{"n":25,"text":"तत्रातुष्यन्त योधाश्च सिद्धाश्चापि दिवि स्थिताः ।\nसुतसोमस्य तत्कर्म दृष्ट्वाश्रद्धेयमद्भुतम् ।\nरथस्थं नृपतिं तं तु पदातिः सन्नयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The warriors and the Siddhas standing in the sky were pleased there, seeing that astonishing deed of Sutasoma, who, on foot, fought the king who stood in a chariot."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्य तीक्ष्णैर्महावेगैर्भल्लैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nव्यहनत्कार्मुकं राजा तूणीरं चैव सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, with sharp, swift broad-headed arrows with smooth joints, shattered his bow and his quiver on all sides."}},{"n":27,"text":"स च्छिन्नधन्वा समरे खड्गमुद्यम्य नानदन् ।\nवैडूर्योत्पलवर्णाभं हस्तिदन्तमयत्सरुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his bow cut, Sutasoma roared in the battle and raised a sword, colored like lapis and blue lotus, with a hilt of ivory."}},{"n":28,"text":"भ्राम्यमाणं ततस्तं तु विमलाम्बरवर्चसम् ।\nकालोपमं ततो मेने सुतसोमस्य धीमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he whirled it, shining like a spotless garment, the wise Sutasoma's sword seemed like Death itself."}},{"n":29,"text":"सोऽचरत्सहसा खड्गी मण्डलानि सहस्रशः ।\nचतुर्विंशन्महाराज शिक्षाबलसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the strength of his training, O great king, he suddenly ranged about in sword-turns, twenty-four times, by the thousands in his skill."}},{"n":30,"text":"सौबलस्तु ततस्तस्य शरांश्चिक्षेप वीर्यवान् ।\nतानापतत एवाशु चिच्छेद परमासिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Subala's son, the mighty Shakuni, shot arrows at him, but Sutasoma cut them with his fine sword as they came."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महाराज सौबलः परवीरहा ।\nप्राहिणोत्सुतसोमस्य शरानाशीविषोपमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O great king, Shakuni, slayer of enemy heroes, in anger sent arrows like venomous snakes at Sutasoma."}},{"n":32,"text":"चिच्छेद तांश्च खड्गेन शिक्षया च बलेन च ।\nदर्शयँल्लाघवं युद्धे तार्क्ष्यवीर्यसमद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showing his lightness of hand in the fight, shining like Garuda in power, Sutasoma cut them with his sword, by skill and strength."}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्य संचरतो राजन्मण्डलावर्तने तदा ।\nक्षुरप्रेण सुतीक्ष्णेन खड्गं चिच्छेद सुप्रभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he moved about, O king, whirling in circles, Shakuni cut his bright sword with a very sharp razor-headed arrow."}},{"n":34,"text":"स च्छिन्नः सहसा भूमौ निपपात महानसिः ।\nअवशस्य स्थितं हस्ते तं खड्गं सत्सरुं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great sword, cut, suddenly fell to the ground, and only the hilt remained in the helpless Sutasoma's hand."}},{"n":35,"text":"छिन्नमाज्ञाय निस्त्रिंशमवप्लुत्य पदानि षट् ।\nप्राविध्यत ततः शेषं सुतसोमो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the sword cut, the great chariot-warrior Sutasoma leapt six paces and flung the remaining part at Shakuni."}},{"n":36,"text":"स च्छित्त्वा सगुणं चापं रणे तस्य महात्मनः ।\nपपात धरणीं तूर्णं स्वर्णवज्रविभूषितः ।\nसुतसोमस्ततोऽगच्छच्छ्रुतकीर्तेर्महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It cut that great soul's bow with its string in the battle and fell swiftly to the ground, decked with gold and diamonds. Then Sutasoma went to Shrutakirti's chariot."}},{"n":37,"text":"सौबलोऽपि धनुर्गृह्य घोरमन्यत्सुदुःसहम् ।\nअभ्ययात्पाण्डवानीकं निघ्नञ्शत्रुगणान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni too took another dreadful and hard-to-withstand bow and went against the Pandava army, killing many groups of enemies."}},{"n":38,"text":"तत्र नादो महानासीत्पाण्डवानां विशां पते ।\nसौबलं समरे दृष्ट्वा विचरन्तमभीतवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry arose among the Pandavas there, O lord of the people, when they saw Subala's son moving about the battle unafraid."}},{"n":39,"text":"तान्यनीकानि दृप्तानि शस्त्रवन्ति महान्ति च ।\nद्राव्यमाणान्यदृश्यन्त सौबलेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those proud, great, armed divisions were seen being driven off by the great-souled Shakuni."}},{"n":40,"text":"यथा दैत्यचमूं राजन्देवराजो ममर्द ह ।\nतथैव पाण्डवीं सेनां सौबलेयो व्यनाशयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the king of the gods crushed the army of the Daityas, so Subala's son destroyed the Pandava army."}},{"n":41,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नं कृपो राजन्वारयामास संयुगे ।\nयथा दृप्तं वने नागं शरभो वारयेद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa held Dhrishtadyumna back in the battle, as a sharabha holds back a proud elephant in the forest."}},{"n":42,"text":"निरुद्धः पार्षतस्तेन गौतमेन बलीयसा ।\nपदात्पदं विचलितुं नाशक्नोत्तत्र भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Held by the strong Gautama, the Prishata prince, O Bharata, could not move even a step there."}},{"n":43,"text":"गौतमस्य वपुर्दृष्ट्वा धृष्टद्युम्नरथं प्रति ।\nवित्रेसुः सर्वभूतानि क्षयं प्राप्तं च मेनिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Gautama's form against Dhrishtadyumna's chariot, all beings trembled and thought him already lost."}},{"n":44,"text":"तत्रावोचन्विमनसो रथिनः सादिनस्तथा ।\nद्रोणस्य निधने नूनं संक्रुद्धो द्विपदां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the chariot-warriors and horsemen, downcast, said, \"Surely the best of men is enraged over Drona's death."}},{"n":45,"text":"शारद्वतो महातेजा दिव्यास्त्रविदुदारधीः ।\nअपि स्वस्ति भवेदद्य धृष्टद्युम्नस्य गौतमात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-spirited son of Sharadvat, who knows divine weapons, is noble-minded. May Dhrishtadyumna be safe today from Gautama!"}},{"n":46,"text":"अपीयं वाहिनी कृत्स्ना मुच्येत महतो भयात् ।\nअप्ययं ब्राह्मणः सर्वान्न नो हन्यात्समागतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"May this whole army be freed from great danger! May this brahmin not kill all of us who have gathered!"}},{"n":47,"text":"यादृशं दृश्यते रूपमन्तकप्रतिमं भृशम् ।\nगमिष्यत्यद्य पदवीं भारद्वाजस्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such a form is seen, utterly like Death's, that today he will follow Bharadvaja's son's path in battle."}},{"n":48,"text":"आचार्यः क्षिप्रहस्तश्च विजयी च सदा युधि ।\nअस्त्रवान्वीर्यसंपन्नः क्रोधेन च समन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The teacher was quick-handed, always victorious in battle, a master of weapons, strong, and full of anger."}},{"n":49,"text":"पार्षतश्च भृशं युद्धे विमुखोऽद्यापि लक्ष्यते ।\nइत्येवं विविधा वाचस्तावकानां परैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the Prishata prince is seen turning away even now.\" Such were the varied words among your men and the enemy."}},{"n":50,"text":"विनिःश्वस्य ततः क्रुद्धः कृपः शारद्वतो नृप ।\nपार्षतं छादयामास निश्चेष्टं सर्वमर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, the angry Kripa, son of Sharadvat, sighed and covered Dhrishtadyumna, who had become helpless, with arrows at every vital spot."}},{"n":51,"text":"स वध्यमानः समरे गौतमेन महात्मना ।\nकर्तव्यं न प्रजानाति मोहितः परमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck in battle by the great-souled Gautama, Dhrishtadyumna, bewildered in that great fight, did not know what to do."}},{"n":52,"text":"तमब्रवीत्ततो यन्ता कच्चित्क्षेमं नु पार्षत ।\nईदृशं व्यसनं युद्धे न ते दृष्टं कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"His charioteer said to him, \"Are you well, son of Prishata? You have never before seen such trouble in battle."}},{"n":53,"text":"दैवयोगात्तु ते बाणा नातरन्मर्मभेदिनः ।\nप्रेषिता द्विजमुख्येन मर्माण्युद्दिश्य सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By luck, those vital-spot-piercing arrows sent from all sides at your vitals by that chief of brahmins did not pass through you."}},{"n":54,"text":"व्यावर्तये तत्र रथं नदीवेगमिवार्णवात् ।\nअवध्यं ब्राह्मणं मन्ये येन ते विक्रमो हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will turn the chariot away, as one turns a river's flow from the sea. I think the brahmin must be unslayable, since he has destroyed your valor.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्ततो राजञ्शनकैरब्रवीद्वचः ।\nमुह्यते मे मनस्तात गात्रे स्वेदश्च जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, Dhrishtadyumna said slowly, \"My mind is confused, my friend, and sweat comes upon my body."}},{"n":56,"text":"वेपथुं च शरीरे मे रोमहर्षं च पश्य वै ।\nवर्जयन्ब्राह्मणं युद्धे शनैर्याहि यतोऽच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"See the trembling in my body and the hair standing on end. Avoid the brahmin in the battle and go slowly where Achyuta is."}},{"n":57,"text":"अर्जुनं भीमसेनं वा समरे प्राप्य सारथे ।\nक्षेममद्य भवेद्यन्तरिति मे नैष्ठिकी मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charioteer, reaching Arjuna or Bhimasena in the battle, I am sure that today we will be safe.\""}},{"n":58,"text":"ततः प्रायान्महाराज सारथिस्त्वरयन्हयान् ।\nयतो भीमो महेष्वासो युयुधे तव सैनिकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O great king, the charioteer urged the horses and went where the mighty bowman Bhima was fighting your soldiers."}},{"n":59,"text":"प्रद्रुतं तु रथं दृष्ट्वा धृष्टद्युम्नस्य मारिष ।\nकिरञ्शरशतान्येव गौतमोऽनुययौ तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Dhrishtadyumna's chariot flee, O sir, Gautama followed, scattering hundreds of arrows."}},{"n":60,"text":"शङ्खं च पूरयामास मुहुर्मुहुररिंदमः ।\nपार्षतं प्राद्रवद्यन्तं महेन्द्र इव शम्बरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The subduer of foes blew his conch again and again, and chased the fleeing Prishata prince as great Indra chased Shambara."}},{"n":61,"text":"शिखण्डिनं तु समरे भीष्ममृत्युं दुरासदम् ।\nहार्दिक्यो वारयामास स्मयन्निव मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hardika, smiling again and again, held back Shikhandi in the battle, he who was hard to approach and was Bhishma's death."}},{"n":62,"text":"शिखण्डी च समासाद्य हृदिकानां महारथम् ।\nपञ्चभिर्निशितैर्भल्लैर्जत्रुदेशे समार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandi, reaching the great chariot-warrior of the Hridikas, struck him in the collarbone with five sharp broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":63,"text":"कृतवर्मा तु संक्रुद्धो भित्त्वा षष्टिभिराशुगैः ।\nधनुरेकेन चिच्छेद हसन्राजन्महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Kritavarman, the great chariot-warrior, angry, pierced him with sixty swift arrows and, laughing, cut his bow with one more."}},{"n":64,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय द्रुपदस्यात्मजो बली ।\nतिष्ठ तिष्ठेति संक्रुद्धो हार्दिक्यं प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty son of Drupada took another bow and, furious, said to Hardika, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":65,"text":"ततोऽस्य नवतिं बाणान्रुक्मपुङ्खान्सुतेजनान् ।\nप्रेषयामास राजेन्द्र तेऽस्याभ्रश्यन्त वर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O best of kings, he sent ninety gold-feathered, very sharp arrows at Kritavarman, and they slipped off his armor."}},{"n":66,"text":"वितथांस्तान्समालक्ष्य पतितांश्च महीतले ।\nक्षुरप्रेण सुतीक्ष्णेन कार्मुकं चिच्छिदे बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them fail and fall to the ground, the strong Kritavarman cut Shikhandi's bow with a very sharp razor-headed arrow."}},{"n":67,"text":"अथैनं छिन्नधन्वानं भग्नशृङ्गमिवर्षभम् ।\nअशीत्या मार्गणैः क्रुद्धो बाह्वोरुरसि चार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, furious, he tormented him, whose bow was cut like a bull with a broken horn, with eighty arrows in the arms and chest."}},{"n":68,"text":"कृतवर्मा तु संक्रुद्धो मार्गणैः कृतविक्षतः ।\nधनुरन्यत्समादाय समार्गणगणं प्रभो ।\nशिखण्डिनं बाणवरैः स्कन्धदेशेऽभ्यताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarman, furious and hurt by the arrows, took another bow with its bundle of arrows, O lord, and struck Shikhandi with fine arrows in the shoulder."}},{"n":69,"text":"स्कन्धदेशे स्थितैर्बाणैः शिखण्डी च रराज ह ।\nशाखाप्रतानैर्विमलैः सुमहान्स यथा द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the arrows lodged in his shoulder, Shikhandi shone like a great tree with bright spreading branches."}},{"n":70,"text":"तावन्योन्यं भृशं विद्ध्वा रुधिरेण समुक्षितौ ।\nअन्योन्यशृङ्गाभिहतौ रेजतुर्वृषभाविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having pierced each other deeply, they were drenched with blood and shone like two bulls that have gored each other with horns."}},{"n":71,"text":"अन्योन्यस्य वधे यत्नं कुर्वाणौ तौ महारथौ ।\nरथाभ्यां चेरतुस्तत्र मण्डलानि सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Striving to kill each other, those two great chariot-warriors moved about there in their chariots in thousands of circles."}},{"n":72,"text":"कृतवर्मा महाराज पार्षतं निशितैः शरैः ।\nरणे विव्याध सप्तत्या स्वर्णपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, Kritavarman in the battle pierced the Prishata's follower Shikhandi with seventy sharp, gold-feathered, stone-sharpened arrows."}},{"n":73,"text":"ततोऽस्य समरे बाणं भोजः प्रहरतां वरः ।\nजीवितान्तकरं घोरं व्यसृजत्त्वरयान्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the battle the Bhoja, best of fighters, hurriedly shot at him a dreadful arrow that could end life."}},{"n":74,"text":"स तेनाभिहतो राजन्मूर्छामाशु समाविशत् ।\nध्वजयष्टिं च सहसा शिश्रिये कश्मलावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by it, O king, Shikhandi quickly fell into a faint and, covered in dizziness, suddenly leaned against his standard-pole."}},{"n":75,"text":"अपोवाह रणात्तं तु सारथी रथिनां वरम् ।\nहार्दिक्यशरसंतप्तं निःश्वसन्तं पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His charioteer carried the best of chariot-warriors out of the fight, scorched by Hardika's arrows and sighing again and again."}},{"n":76,"text":"पराजिते ततः शूरे द्रुपदस्य सुते प्रभो ।\nप्राद्रवत्पाण्डवी सेना वध्यमाना समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the Drupada prince, the brave one, was defeated, the Pandava army, struck on every side, fled."}}]}]}